# `cpp` is external: haskell source can carry C preprocessor lines, and the
# scanner has to hand a whole line to a node that the layout algorithm then
# has to ignore. The directive is one node ending at the newline, and the
# binding after it is unaffected - `main` still starts a declaration.
roots 1
mends 0
holds cpp
spans cpp 0 15
holds bind
spans bind 16 34
